        "reasons": "Nine written acceptances at $650 per round from nine licensed shellfish farms are on the opening (real purchase commitments by these buyers, not a benchmark). The recorded fulfiller is Tidewater Analytical Labs on a written quote of $380 per round including courier, invoiced net 30, and the plan's delivery performer is that fulfiller. Contribution recomputed: 9 x $650 = $5,850 minus 9 x $380 = $3,420 gives $2,430 >= $2,000 target, with $430 headroom (the target still holds if one farm drops: 8 x $270 = $2,160). Net-30 supplier terms with farm cash settling day 17 keep peak exposure at $0, so the no-up-front-capital term holds; the plan subtracts the supplier cost inside the window (day 28) even though it would fall due later, which is the conservative way to count contribution. Settlement 12 days (EVIDENCE) from day-5 invoicing gives day 17 inside 30. The cage-set exclusion is a real constraint: Bay Gear must be paid $1,020 before shipment, which no evidence can fit under a $0 exposure cap.",
        "findings": [
          "Delivery timing: the plan has Tidewater collect and test on day 3 and invoicing on day 5; no lab turnaround is recorded, but the 12-day time-to-cash evidence and 13 days of slack cover it. Confirm round dates with Tidewater on day 1.",
